  "hypotheses": [
    {
      "id": "H-01",
      "text": "A newcomer can say what Change Fabric is (a layer on the agent they already use) and whether it is for them after one viewing.",
      "dimension": "role"
    },
    {
      "id": "H-02",
      "text": "Scenes that follow the homepage's headings and order (the problem, Is it for me?, What is it?, Before it merges, Start building) make the page and the clip read as one story.",
      "dimension": "look_and_feel"
    }
  ],
  "review": {
    "kind": "explainer",
    "audience": "Newcomers moving into engineering who already use AI tools for code, for example from marketing technology, deciding from the homepage whether the toolkit is for them",
    "purpose": [
      "Your agent writes code faster than you can judge it, and you can't yet tell whether it is good or safe to ship",
      "If you already ask an agent to write code, it is for you, inside Claude Code, Codex CLI, Copilot CLI, OpenCode or Pi",
      "Your coding agent is the harness and Change Fabric extends it with rubrics, commands and hooks, whose rubrics credit sources such as Sandi Metz and Martin Fowler",
      "One CHANGE.md adds a gate where five checks run and any failure blocks the merge, and you do not need it on day one",
      "How to start: brew tap, brew install change-fabric and change-fabric-install, open your agent, watch a rubric apply, then Start Building"
    ]
  },
